#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186063953 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "89f65f58-bd3d-5c3f-b9e0-462d74d75b59" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Second Order Derivatives"}] :question/id #uuid "0bc72287-b782-5add-89ef-f2a465573ab0" :question/is-example true :question/math-academy-id "e-3653" :question/problem "Find $f''(x)$ for $f(x) = 2x^3 + \\dfrac 1 x$." :question/worked-solution "Computing the first derivative, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf^{′}(x) &= (2x^{3} + \\frac{1}{x})^{′} \\\\\n&= (2x^{3} + x^{-1})^{′} \\\\\n&= 2(3)x^{2} - x^{-2} \\\\\n&= 6x^{2} - x^{-2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the second derivative, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf^{″}(x) &= (6x^{2} - x^{-2})^{′} \\\\\n&= 6(2)x - (-2)x^{-3} \\\\\n&= 12x + 2x^{-3}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186063954 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6afb4058-908a-5983-9c1e-78ee3fbadf44" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Second Order Derivatives Using Leibnitz Notation"}] :question/id #uuid "b092bc79-d369-5ff0-a6bb-5fc059699275" :question/is-example true :question/math-academy-id "e-3654" :question/problem "Calculate $\\dfrac {\\textrm d^2 y}{\\textrm d x^2}$ for $y = 3 x^4 + 5x+ \\sqrt x$." :question/worked-solution "Computing the first derivative, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{dy}{dx} &= \\frac{d}{dx}(3x^{4} + 5x + \\sqrt{x}) \\\\\n&= \\frac{d}{dx}(3x^{4} + 5x + x^{1/2}) \\\\\n&= 3(4)x^{3} + 5 + \\frac{1}{2}x^{-1/2} \\\\\n&= 12x^{3} + 5 + \\frac{1}{2}x^{-1/2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the second derivative, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{d^{2}y}{dx^{2}} &= \\frac{d}{dx}(12x^{3} + 5 + \\frac{1}{2}x^{-1/2}) \\\\\n&= 12(3)x^{2} + 0 + \\frac{1}{2}(-\\frac{1}{2})x^{-3/2} \\\\\n&= 36x^{2} - \\frac{1}{4}x^{-3/2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186063955 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "322168bb-52e3-5352-a2e3-c5bdbf2bc13e" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Higher Order Derivatives"}] :question/id #uuid "627f1ef4-64a8-5764-89c7-cb4e31009dbe" :question/is-example true :question/math-academy-id "e-3655" :question/problem "Given $y = \\dfrac {3 x^2 + x - 1} x$, find $\\dfrac {\\textrm d^{3} y} {\\textrm d x^3}$." :question/worked-solution "First, notice that we can rewrite the function as the sum of powers of $x$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny &= \\frac{3x^{2} + x - 1}{x} \\\\\n&= \\frac{3x^{2}}{x} + \\frac{x}{x} - \\frac{1}{x} \\\\\n&= 3x + 1 - x^{-1}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, computing the first derivative, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{dy}{dx} &= \\frac{d}{dx}(3x + 1 - x^{-1}) \\\\\n&= 3 + 0 - (-1)x^{-2} \\\\\n&= 3 + x^{-2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the second derivative, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{d^{2}y}{dx^{2}} &= \\frac{d}{dx}(3 + x^{-2}) \\\\\n&= 0 + (-2)x^{-3} \\\\\n&=-2x^{-3}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, computing the third derivative, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{d^{3}y}{dx^{3}} &= \\frac{d}{dx}(-2x^{-3}) \\\\\n&=-2(-3)x^{-4} \\\\\n&= 6x^{-4}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064386 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6afb4058-908a-5983-9c1e-78ee3fbadf44" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Second Order Derivatives Using Leibnitz Notation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f77246d2-bf58-519a-bbaf-ee09cdb86d59" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "60x^{2} + 8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061001} {:answer/id #uuid "fb658a6f-2c8e-5660-be3f-55653f958ed8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "60x^{2} + 12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061002} {:answer/id #uuid "28e3a2fd-855c-5325-beb9-f4fdb154f5ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "60x^{2} + 8x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061003} {:answer/id #uuid "3ba93afd-1f36-569a-ad56-214b680c4d32" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "60x^{3} + 8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061004} {:answer/id #uuid "